item.text:
Implemented in `app/page.tsx` using Next.js’s recommended dynamic rendering API:

```tsx
import { connection } from 'next/server';

export default async function Home() {
  await connection();
  const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Server Timestamp</h1>
      <p>Current server time: {timestamp}</p>
    </main>
  );
}
```

This uses `await connection()` to opt out of static prerendering without cookies/headers, so the timestamp is generated on every request. I also verified with `npm run build`; `/` is reported as `ƒ (Dynamic)` (server-rendered on demand).
